==Portuguese==
{{wikipedia|lang=pt}}
[[Image:Surface anatomy of the heart.png|thumb|200px|o coração]]

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|pt|roa-opt|coraçon||heart}}, from a derivative of {{inh|pt|la|cor||heart}} with the suffix {{m|pt|-ção|-ação}}, either through a {{inh|pt|VL.|-}} root {{m|la|*corātiō}}, {{m|la|*corātiōne}} or {{m|la||*coraceōne}}. Ultimately from {{inh|pt|itc-pro|*kord}}, from {{inh|pt|ine-pro|*ḱḗr}} ~ {{m|ine-pro||*ḱr̥d-}}.

Cognate with {{cog|an|corazón}}, {{cog|ast|corazón}}, {{cog|gl|corazón}}, {{cog|lad|korasón}}, {{cog|roa-leo|corazón}}, {{cog|mwl|coraçon}}, {{cog|mxi|corachón}} and {{cog|es|corazón}} (Old Spanish {{m|osp|coraçon}}).

====Pronunciation====
* {{a|Portugal}} {{IPA|pt|/ku.ɾɐ.ˈsɐ̃w̃/}}
* {{a|Brazil}} {{IPA|pt|/ko.ɾa.ˈsɐ̃w̃/}}
* {{hyphenation|pt|co|ra|ção}}
* {{homophones|pt|curação|Curação}} (Portugal)
* {{audio|pt|pt-pt-coração.ogg|Audio}} (Portugal)

